{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999/events","html_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/21999","id":294039053,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyOTQwMzkwNTM=","number":21999,"title":".pipe operators on EventEmitter leaks subscriptions","user":{"login":"jbedard","id":89246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard","html_url":"https://github.com/jbedard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbedard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":130606843,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzA2MDY4NDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/type:%20bug/fix","name":"type: bug/fix","color":"EEEEEE","default":false,"description":null},{"id":375497160,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzU0OTcxNjA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/freq2:%20medium","name":"freq2: medium","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":null},{"id":375498062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzU0OTgwNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/memory%20leak","name":"memory leak","color":"dcf26d","default":false,"description":"Issue related to a memory leak"},{"id":375501288,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzU1MDEyODg=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/labels/area:%20core","name":"area: core","color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the framework runtime"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2018-02-02T22:10:36Z","updated_at":"2019-09-13T06:51:45Z","closed_at":"2018-02-06T15:57:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## I'm submitting a...\r\n<pre><code>[X] Bug report</code></pre>\r\n\r\n## Current behavior\r\n`EventEmitter` overrides `Subject.subscribe` to add `isAsync` support but doesn't take all `Subject.subscribe` param types into account. In this case `FilterSubscriber` (and probably other `Subscriber` types) filters correctly but does not cleanup on unsubscribe.\r\n\r\n## Expected behavior\r\nMethods available on `EventEmitter` should function and not leak.\r\n\r\n## Minimal reproduction of the problem with instructions\r\n```\r\nit('should have no observers after .pipe(op).subscribe().unsubscribe()', () => {\r\n  const ee = new EventEmitter();\r\n  ee.pipe(filter(() => true)).subscribe().unsubscribe();\r\n  expect(ee.observers.length).toBe(0);\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n## What is the motivation / use case for changing the behavior?\r\nWhile I don't think this is a standard (or supported?) use case of `EventEmitter`, there are definitely [some use cases](https://github.com/valor-software/ng2-dragula/blob/v1.3.1/src/components/dragula.provider.ts#L6) out there. Or people could potentially be listening to outputs within their own components etc. Either way, if the standard `Subject` methods are available they should probably function correctly and not leak.\r\n\r\nChanging `EventEmitter` to not extend `Subject` would be another solution which I know has been mentioned before.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"alxhub","id":4175141,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzUxNDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4175141?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub","html_url":"https://github.com/alxhub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alxhub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21999/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}